  "findings": [
    "Main new-coordinate discovery counts and AUC improve over static historical ranking, random, space filling, target-only GP and nearest-source residual adaptation under the registered individual paired intervals.",
    "FSBO has higher main-condition collision counts and AUC; both history_response-minus-FSBO intervals are negative. Pooled-FT count differences include zero.",
    "Mean behavior coverage is highest for history_response in the main condition, but its difference from FSBO includes zero; equal-count curves and censored runs are retained.",
    "Historical-set-specific discoveries improve over historical ranking, but target-only GP discovers more such collisions than history_response. Version-new and history-specific labels remain distinct and source-set dependent.",
    "Strict-family findings do not establish superiority over FSBO or target-only GP.",
    "The response-correlation ablation supports a small early-discovery AUC gain; weight adaptation, independent target component and finite lookahead do not show stable standalone discovery gains in the registered mechanism tasks.",
    "Source mismatch effects vary by family; changes in mixture weights alone do not establish correction of negative transfer.",
    "Measured replay process and selected-scenario equivalent execution costs remain separate; no total amortized speedup is inferred."
  ],
